  "note": "Named shot views (Latch). 009-*: brief 009 C crossings (the Records Office front crossing, orbit-walk/2, at play zoom, at eye level from the square kerb and from above for the arc yaw; a refuge crossing on market-street; the cafe's crossings north-west of the home square at play zoom). One camera per view under cameras/, rendered by Shots to out/shots/<prefix>-<name>.png. projection: top (orthographic, straight down, north up, fits `frame`), export (the export's `view`: yaw, pitch, zoom, focus; optional `zoom` overrides the ortho size, `focus` = an element id whose top centre is the focus, `street` = a street name: focus on the shopfront there with the most others within `radius` m, default 40), perspective (yaw compass degrees, 90 = looking east; pitch degrees below horizontal; fits `frame`, or stands at `eye` [x, y, height] looking at `look` [x, y, height] (plan frame; on an export view `look` is the focus), or stands on `along` (a road or foot line) at fraction `at` of its first segment, `side` m to its right, eyeHeight above it, looking down the segment). frame: layer names or element ids, '*' = the whole build, or `kind@x,y` = the street item of that kind within 3 m of that plan point (street item ids renumber whenever street furniture changes: name street items by place, never by id). shadowDistance (m) is applied to the URP asset while the view renders (absent = the asset default; 1 = effectively none, 0 is ignored by URP); fog toggles RenderSettings.fog; clear = look.json entry for the background. Glint tunes.",
